## What this project teaches

- Encrypting data with AES-GCM and managing a key outside the code
- Generating unguessable IDs with `crypto/rand`
- Making an operation happen exactly once under concurrency
- Designing safe HTTP semantics (why reading is a POST)
- Background goroutines for cleanup
- Testing HTTP handlers with `httptest`, including table-driven and concurrent tests
- Building a React interface with Tailwind CSS and Vite, and serving the build from Go with `embed`
- Hardening the pages with security headers and a Content Security Policy
- Using MongoDB TTL indexes for automatic expiry, and an atomic find-and-delete for the read-once guarantee
- Writing one set of tests that runs against two storage implementations